item.description:
arXiv:2608.21104v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: Let $\alpha>-1/2$, $\alpha
e0$, and let $$ \Delta_\alpha=- rac{d^2}{dx^2}- rac{2\alpha}{x} rac{d}{dx} $$ be the Bessel operator on $\mathbb R_+=(0,\infty)$. We characterize boundedness and compactness of commutators of $R_\alpha= rac{d}{dx}\Delta_\alpha^{-1/2}$ on the Andersen--Kerman two-weight setting. For $1<p<\infty$ and $\mu,\lambda\in A_{p,\alpha}$, put $ 
u=\left( rac{\mu}{\lambda}ight)^{1/p}, \ dho_\alpha(x)=x^{2\alpha+1}\,dx. $ For real-valued symbols, $$ \|[b,R_\alpha]\|_{L^p(\mu\,dx)	o L^p(\lambda\,dx)} \simeq \|b\|_{m{BMO}_{
u,\alpha}}, $$ where the Bloom oscillation is computed with respect to $dho_\alpha$. Moreover $$ [b,R_\alpha]:L^p(\mu\,dx)	o L^p(\lambda\,dx) 	ext{ is compact} \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad b\inm{VMO}_{
u,\alpha}. $$ The proof uses the exact conjugation $ U_w(x)=x^{p-2\alpha-1}w(x), \ [U_w]_{A_p(ho_\alpha)}=[w]_{A_{p,\alpha}}, $ which transfers the problem to the quotient Bessel kernel on $(\mathbb R_+,|x-y|,ho_\alpha)$. We isolate the required Calder'on--Zygmund estimates and one-sided non-degeneracy in this quotient normalization. The measure $dho_\alpha$ is distinct from the usual Bessel measure $dm_\alpha=x^{2\alpha}\,dx$. It is the Bloom base measure selected by the Andersen--Kerman conjugation and is used throughout the two-weight theory below.
